          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What is osteoarthritis, and is it the same thing as arthritis?",
          "answer": "Osteoarthritis is a disorder that affects the entire joint, including the cartilage, the bone underneath, ligaments, the joint lining, and surrounding muscles. In this condition, the cartilage is gradually lost, and the underlying bone changes in response. It commonly affects the knees, hips, hands, and spine (condition-osteoarthritis). It is more complex than simple \"wear and tear,\" as it involves active processes like inflammation and attempted repair (condition-osteoarthritis).\n\nArthritis is a broader term for conditions that involve inflammation or degeneration of one or more joints. Osteoarthritis is a specific type of arthritis. Other types of arthritis include infectious arthropathies and inflammatory polyarthropathies, such as rheumatoid arthritis and gout (coding-icd10-chapter-13-musculoskeletal). Therefore, osteoarthritis is not the same thing as arthritis, but rather one form of it.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
